  "notes": "Electricity ~35-45% of smelter cash cost, alumina ~30-36% (Antaike 2021). GCC smelters (6.16 Mt, ~8.3% of world) run on gas-fired power; anodes use petroleum coke. LME ~$3,157/t on 27 Feb 2026, $3,544 on 9 Mar, ~$3,585 on 31 Mar after the 28 Mar strikes on Alba and EGA Al Taweelah, $3,787.5 four-year high in early June, ~$3,273 Sep average. Qatalum ~60%; Alba cut 19% of capacity. No published oil-to-aluminium pass-through found (asked of Seb in OXH-5).",
